<resources>
    <!--
      The launcher icon takes its paint from the wallpaper, like every other
      surface in the app. These are the platform's own dynamic palette, public
      since API 31, and minSdk is 31, so there is no fallback to maintain.

      Referenced from the adaptive icon rather than baked into the vector, so
      the icon follows the wallpaper whether or not themed icons are switched
      on in the launcher. A themed icon tints the monochrome layer itself and
      ignores these, which is why both paths end up correct.

      600 against 0: a mid tone of the accent under a near white glyph. That
      pair keeps its contrast on every wallpaper, which a lighter background
      would not.
    -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">@android:color/system_accent1_600</color>
    <color name="ic_launcher_glyph">@android:color/system_accent1_0</color>
</resources>
